Someone wrote the on and off thresholds the wrong way round by mistake. The light is steady and analogRead(A1) always reads 480. When this code runs, what does the LED on D13 do?

```
const int ACMA = 523;
const int KAPAMA = 423;
bool yanik = false;

void loop() {
  int d = analogRead(A1);
  if (!yanik && d < ACMA) yanik = true;
  else if (yanik && d > KAPAMA) yanik = false;
  digitalWrite(13, yanik);
}
```

